  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole and launched in Q3 2023. The project has received a $2M budget approval and is currently in Phase Two, where the team achieved a breakthrough in predictive analytics. To support this progress, the team expanded by adding five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. The project is also exploring AI partnerships with TechInnovate and has updated security protocols, including multi-factor authentication. Stakeholder feedback on the prototype is being sought, and a detailed progress report will be presented on November 20th."
